{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471235-immunity-to-sunlight","id":1471235,"title":"Immunity to sunlight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-25T05:35:46-08:00","id":1471235,"title":"Immunity to sunlight","content":"As far as I know, 15th generation vampires gets lethal damage instead of aggravated.<br /> I've found nothing about the rarest-than-rare 16th generation. Mabye they take bashing damage, or lethal but reduced by 1?<br /> <br /> Fortitude can help, obviously, but a 15th generation is limited to 3 dots ( and a 16th to 2 ).<br /> But there's an exception. Golconda.<br /> <br /> So, mabye a 16th generation who reached Golconda, with Stamina 5 and 8-9 dots in Resilience, could be almost immune to sunlight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T09:41:35-08:00","id":1471240,"title":"","content":"In theory, yeah. But a 16th Gen vampire reaching Golconda and getting super high Attributes and Disciplines like that is like EXTREMELY unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T12:40:32-08:00","id":1471243,"title":"","content":"The math of V20 (assuming V20, wasn't specified) that no amount of dice is ever going to make a vampire immune to sunlight. Both sun and fire damage work in a unique way: they do relatively small sets amount of direct damage, but the soak difficulty is variable. A vampire with 15 dice to soak against sunlight trying to run around nude in is direct sunlight? They need 3 successes at difficulty 10 to avoid any damage, every three seconds. The odds are very much against them lasting 4 rounds. Difficulty 10 is just hell (esp. for an Attribute only roll like soak) for any hopes of succeeding just through tossing a ridiculously large dice-pool. Even vampires that achieve really high soak pools against sunlight need to take some steps protect themselves from the sun to keep the difficulty of the roll down, or they're going to get crispy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T14:54:30-08:00","id":1471245,"title":"","content":"Get yourself ten dots in thaumaturgy and you can get immune to sunlight for a year... ;P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T15:14:20-08:00","id":1471247,"title":"","content":"Well, mabye you can take a Stamina specialization ( soaking damage; or, if it need to be more specific, soaking sunlight damage ) and get double success for each 10.<br /> There's the Tough as Nails merit ( a<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:rubik\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">ll soak rolls are made at -1 difficulty ).<br /> Daredevil merit gives 3 extra dices for risky ( at least 3 lethal damage ) and difficult ( 8 or more ) actions, more importantly it negates 1 botch.<br /> Then there is that slightly OP Merit, Legendary Attribute, who allows to raise an attribute to 6 and gives a custom special power related to that area. Our vampire could have Stamina 6 and the difficulty of rolls to soak damage reduced by 2.<br /> <br /> To make things easier there's also the option &quot;full clothing, cloak and sunglasses&quot; who reduces Difficulty to 5. Mabye an extra-thick fabric and maximum protection sunlotion may reduce it to 4.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> But the initial idea was less about mechanic and more that a vampire looks - and feels - more alive the higher his humanity. In V5 humanity 10 allows a saintly vampire to get only bashing damage from sunlight. 15th generation vampires, according to Beckett diary, are almost alive themselves, they show a tiny amound of beard and nail grow, cellular replication, sometimes thay can even have child. Golconda means partially trascending the Curse too.<br /> <br /> So, a 15th generation Humanity 10 who reached Golconda would be... more a live immortal than undead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 12-25-2021, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-25T15:26:11-08:00","id":1471249,"title":"","content":"16th Generation vampires are dealt lethal damage from sunlight just like 15th Generation. The difference is that 16th Generation can attempt to soak Sunlight lethal damage with Stamina, which is not stated for 15th Gen making me assume that they can heal Sunlight damage like lethal but soak it like aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":". 12-25-2021, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T05:41:50-08:00","id":1471273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471235-immunity-to-sunlight?p=1471247#post1471247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, mabye you can take a Stamina specialization ( soaking damage)</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a player try this at one of my games. <br /> My thoughts were &quot;get the fuck off my table&quot; (but of course, being diplomatic I just said that wouldn't work and that he should come up with something new) <br /> <br /> Odd thoughts but would the dice limit for opperating during the day effect soak? <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T12:34:47-08:00","id":1471293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471235-immunity-to-sunlight?p=1471247#post1471247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, mabye you can take a Stamina specialization ( soaking damage; or, if it need to be more specific, soaking sunlight damage ) and get double success for each 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to apply a specialty to damage or soak are fairly contentious things.<br /> <br /> That said, 15 dice, diff 10? A specialty is both a massive improvement, and still far from &quot;immunity.&quot; You've gone from ~7% odds of soaking all the damage each roll to ~33%. You vampire will still be taking damage, rapidly, even if most likely not a full 3 every turn. It would be a statistical miracle for them to last 30 seconds unprotected in direct sunlight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's the Tough as Nails merit. </div> </div> </div>So, your ST lets a specialty apply, you've racked up 15 soak dice, and you're now at diff 9. You have a mighty 55% chance of soaking all 3 levels of damage per roll. If the dice love you, you might survive doing something significant out of combat time, like changing a flat tire, before the damage gets too high for you to bear. Still far from what people would consider immunity even if we're getting closer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Daredevil </div> </div> </div>I think letting this apply to the soak roll from the repercussions of your risky actions is pushing the intended use of this Merit even if I can't say it's absolutely wrong to use it this way by the rules. The Merit is supposed to give you +3 dice and remove one 1 rolled from counting against you on an action you take that's risky (defined by high difficulty and risk of damage). My example of a vampire trying to change a flat tire in sunlight might count for the Craft roll (the risky action) but not the soak roll. Daredevils might do some crazy shit, and when they pull it off it's amazing, but if they still miss... they tend to get hurt bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then there is that slightly OP Merit, Legendary Attribute... </div> </div> </div>I think we're getting a bit off course when we're grabbing Mage Merits for your VtM hypothetical builds. I mean, yes, I get the idea of trying to figure out every last possible part of the system to see what the true limits are, but to me when you start getting to the point of bending to this level, you undermine the point of the exercise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To make things easier there's also the option &quot;full clothing, cloak and sunglasses&quot; who reduces Difficulty to 5. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was always an option. But this is the sunlight equivalent of wearing armor, or having bullet resistant windows between you and a shooter. You're not immune to the damage, you're putting material between you and the source of the damage.<br /> <br /> If you see someone wearing full plate armor get shot at with an arrow, and the arrow just bounces off the chest plate, you don't go, &quot;Wow, they're immune to arrows!&quot; you go, &quot;Wow, that's some quality armor!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the initial idea was less about mechanic and more that a vampire looks - and feels - more alive the higher his humanity. </div> </div> </div>High Humanity has bonuses for this, they're just limited. And burning up in sunlight drastically reduces the feeling of being more alive at higher Humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In V5 humanity 10 allows a saintly vampire to get only bashing damage from sunlight. 15th generation vampires, according to Beckett diary, are almost alive themselves, they show a tiny amound of beard and nail grow, cellular replication, sometimes thay can even have child. Golconda means partially trascending the Curse too.<br /> <br /> So, a 15th generation Humanity 10 who reached Golconda would be... more a live immortal than undead? </div> </div> </div>Requiem 2e also makes high Humanity much easier on dealing with sunlight. It's almost like later games felt like, yes, the promise of high Humanity (Golconda or not) to be a bit more tempting to vampires that want to feel human. Though it's worth noting that V5 only has two levels of damage, superficial and aggravated; rather than the three tier system older WoD and the CofD games use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471235-immunity-to-sunlight?p=1471273#post1471273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd thoughts but would the dice limit for opperating during the day effect soak?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't... but as far as I can tell a technical reading of V20 would apply the dice limit to soak. It doesn't except reflexive actions.<br /> <br /> Of course, any vampire that's going to spend enough time awake during daylight to worry about building themselves up to endure it is probably going to want the Light Sleeper Merit to ignore this anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-26T12:54:59-08:00","id":1471294,"title":"","content":"Humanity 10 in V5 takes halved aggravated damage, not Superficial (Bashing damage is not a thing in this edition). A Vampire with Blood Potency 1 would take only 1 aggravated damage per turn this way, instead of 2. Obscured Sunlight reduces the damage to every other turn.<br /> <br /> Since it has been brought up, normal Thinblood take only 1 point of superficial per turn, and like full vampires, can reduce it to every other turn by obscuring it. Day Drinker Thinbloods can walk in the sunlight without issues, besides their health tracker being halved and they loosing access to the powers of the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T10:12:37-08:00","id":1471340,"title":"","content":"Would the merit Discipline Prodigy Fortitude drop the target number by one for soaking damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-27T10:54:41-08:00","id":1471341,"title":"","content":"It's debatable. IIRC the wording reads technically as only applying to activating the powers, which means it does nothing for Disciplines that grant bonuses without rolling first.<br /> <br /> While letting it work for rolls boosted by such Disciplines (like soak and Fortitude) has a compelling amount of sense to it, Celerity and Protean esp. get pretty crazy with a flat -1 to any roll boosted by those Disciplines as they're much broader in application and utility than Potence and Fortitude are.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T10:29:05-08:00","id":1471397,"title":"","content":"I see the trouble with something like Celerity. Why not just make up a merit.<br /> <br /> You could have a 7 point merit called sunscreen or something that lowers the target number to soak sunlight damage by 3. I don't think it would come up all that much and standing naked on a clear day at noon will still kill you. Or maybe an expensive merit that makes sunlight damage lethal instead of aggravated? again I don't see it coming up all that often anyway. It is extremely difficult to stay awake during the day as it is.<br /> <br /> Rules are fluid as long as everyone agrees.<br /> <br /> I should add my thoughts on dice pools during the day, I think it all comes down to fatigue affecting your motor skills and such, but I wouldn't apply it to soaking damage. Most elders have around a 3 humanity, a mage or even a human with a bottle of lighter fluid and a match could wipe one out with little effort if that was the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24221,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","user":"Vamps Like Us","date":". 12-28-2021, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T12:35:38-08:00","id":1471402,"title":"","content":"The tone you want to set is going to matter. The original Dracula novel has Dracula go down in basically normal combat like a human because he's weak; he doesn't burn up in sunlight. The idea of hunters staking an elder vampire in VtM would be fairly impossible if they can toss their full Stamina + Fortitude soak against the staking attempt.<br /> <br /> So there's arguments towards either direction on this. Go with what fits your wants for the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-28T12:48:00-08:00","id":1471403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471235-immunity-to-sunlight?p=1471293#post1471293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you might survive doing something significant out of combat time, like changing a flat tire, before the damage gets too high for you to bear. Still far from what people would consider immunity even if we're getting closer.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about changing this tire while naked under direct sunlight at noon, I have to say that <b>I</b> am not immune to sunlight, give me that Daredevil or I may burn before this is over...<br /> <br /> Now, my personal interpretation would be to allow most of the proposed things. Some would need a more strict definition, but <i>sunlight</i> is strict enough. Even if they're stretching the RAW and the most common interpretations, they're still, strictly speaking, RAW.<br /> <br /> So, lets say a Golconda vampire with Gen 16th, Stamina 6, Fortitude 9, Specialization (soaking <b><u>sunlight</u></b> damage), Tough as Nails and Legendary Attribute: Stamina (Day Walker). I wouldn't let Daredevil affect the Stamina roll, but I don't have a problem with cross-splating Legendary Attribute. Maybe -2 dif, maybe -1, or downgrading sunlight damage to Bashing.<br /> <br /> And this is still not immunity, but I don't see a problem with this vampire. Yes, this is 15 dice to soak direct sunlight, maybe at diff 7. Yet this is a humongous expense in resources just for this single feat, two of them only for that, period (Specialization and LA), and this is a heck of an optimized character to do just that, so why bother? This is the least impressive thing a 16th Gen <b>on Golconda with Fortitude 9</b> can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}